      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As a risk analyst, you should look for indicators like increasing commercial vacancy rates and declining foot traffic as primary signals of instability. Shifts in local demographics, such as an outflow of established businesses or an increase in non-local ownership, can also foreshadow economic weakness. Furthermore, monitoring changes in local municipal investment or crime rates provides vital insight into the long-term perceived and actual health of the community. These environmental clues help transition a portfolio review from mere financial statements to forward-looking risk assessment.",
